message: "If you use or discuss this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Prefactor Coefficient Laws for the Gauss-Legendre AGM Algorithm"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Baker
    given-names: Wayne
date-released: 2026-09-21
version: preprint-v2
repository-code: "https://github.com/CWBaker360/agm-prefactor-coefficient-law"
url: "https://github.com/CWBaker360/agm-prefactor-coefficient-law"
abstract: >-
  This paper studies fitted correction coefficients for the Gauss-Legendre
  AGM algorithm. It proves that alpha_(n+1)/alpha_n^2 tends to one half and
  derives an analytic numerator-channel prefactor law for beta_n, including
  the scaled limit -pi*2^(n+1)*beta_(n+1)/beta_n^2 -> 1. Both results follow
  from Brent's theta-function formulas and explicit prefactor asymptotics.
keywords:
  - Gauss-Legendre algorithm
  - arithmetic-geometric mean
  - pi
  - theta functions
  - asymptotic analysis
  - numerical verification
  - Aitken delta-squared process
